content Analyze sensitivity to EMA warmup period (samples parameter).
	
	## Goal
	Find optimal warmup period for spread baseline EMA.
	
	## Current Behavior
	- samples=7000 means ~7000 ticks before trading starts
	- Too short: noisy baseline, bad signals
	- Too long: miss early opportunities, slow adaptation
	
	## Experiment
	- Test samples = {1000, 3000, 5000, 7000, 10000, 15000}
	- Measure: time to first trade, Sharpe, profit
	
	## Questions
	- Is 7000 optimal across all coins?
	- Does optimal samples depend on volatility?
	- Should samples be time-based instead of count-based?
